# Title: Potential Suspicious Browser Launch From Document Reader Process
# ID: 1193d960-2369-499f-a158-7b50a31df682
# Status: test
# Level: medium
# Author: Joseph Kamau
# Date: 2024-05-27
# Tags: attack.execution, attack.t1204.002
# Description: Detects when a browser process or browser tab is launched from an application that handles document files such as Adobe, Microsoft Office, etc. And connects to a web application over http(s), this could indicate a possible phishing attempt.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

index=* eventtype=wineventlog (((parent_process_path="*Acrobat Reader*" OR parent_process_path="*Microsoft Office*" OR parent_process_path="*PDF Reader*") AND (process_path="*\\brave.exe" OR process_path="*\\chrome.exe" OR process_path="*\\firefox.exe" OR process_path="*\\msedge.exe" OR process_path="*\\opera.exe" OR process_path="*\\maxthon.exe" OR process_path="*\\seamonkey.exe" OR process_path="*\\vivaldi.exe") AND process_exec="*http*") AND NOT ((process_exec="*https://go.microsoft.com/fwlink/*")) AND NOT (((process_exec="*http://ad.foxitsoftware.com/adlog.php?*" OR process_exec="*https://globe-map.foxitservice.com/go.php?do=redirect*"))))
